            <ArticleTitle>[Level of knowledge about asthma among parents of asthmatic children].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the level of knowledge of asthma in asthmatic children's parents.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A questionnaire was applied in asthmatic children's parents that had not taken some course about asthma, to explore the knowledge that they have about the illness. A questionnaire of the National Asthma Education Program of NIH was used. They were only questions of false or true options.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">512 questionnaires were applied finding mainly that 53.1% considered to the asthma an emotional illness, 52.5% believed that the way that parents raise their children cause the asthma, 32.8% considered that the acute episodes are not dangerous. The 39.1% ignored that it is possible to measure the lung function, 23.4% considered that the patient with asthma should not carry out exercise and 57.8% &quot;knew&quot; that the asthma in the children disappears spontaneously in the adolescence.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The level of education about asthma in the parents is insufficient, and also is wrong in almost half of them.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
